<title>GERMANY: W.German Oct industry output falls 1.7 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>W.German Oct industry output falls 1.7 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> W.GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT    Oct 96    Sept 96     Oct 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)   -1.7	 -0.3	 -2.0</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     -0.3	 -0.6	  n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		93.6	 95.2	 93.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank statistics.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				     Oct 96		 Sept 96</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Mining		     84.0	 +1.1     83.1	 -1.0</p>
<p> Manufacturing output   93.1	 -1.7     94.7	 -0.4</p>
<p> Incl:Intermed. goods   97.1	 -1.5     98.6	 -0.1</p>
<p>	Capital goods     93.2	 -1.9     95.0	 +1.9</p>
<p>	Consumer durables 80.7	 -2.2     82.5	 -9.0</p>
<p>	Consumer goods    89.8	 -1.5     91.2	 -0.7</p>
<p> Energy output	   104.5	 -0.1    104.6	 -5.1</p>
<p> Construction	     93.8	 -3.0     96.8	 +2.2</p>
<p>Two month comparison Sept/Oct 96 with July/Aug 96:</p>
<p>    Industrial production	    -1.5</p>
<p>Two month comparison Sept/Oct 96 with Sept/Oct 95:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     +0.2</p>
<p> Mining				    -4.8</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		 +0.8</p>
<p>  Including:Intermediate goods     -0.3</p>
<p>		Capital goods	    +3.6</p>
<p>		Consumer durables	+2.1</p>
<p>		Consumer goods	   -1.4</p>
<p> Energy output			   +2.7</p>
<p> Construction			    -6.4</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
